  "full_response": "Below is a sample git commit message along with a diff that illustrates a developer removing hardcoded credentials from the source code and moving them to environment variables:\n\n### Commit Message\n```\nRefactor: Remove hardcoded credentials and use environment variables\n\nThis change improves security by removing sensitive information (such as API keys and passwords) directly from the source code. Instead, these credentials are now accessed via environment variables, allowing easier updates and minimizing risk of accidental exposure. Please ensure you set the corresponding environment variables:\n\n- `API_KEY`: The API key for accessing the external service.\n- `DB_PASSWORD`: The password for the database connection.\n\nNote: After this change, make sure the environment variables are configured in your deployment pipeline or local development setup.\n```\n\n### Diff\n```diff\ndiff --git a/main.py b/main.py\nindex e1a2b3c..d4e5f6g 100644\n--- a/main.py\n+++ b/main.py\n@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@\n import os\n\n # Old hardcoded credential examples\n-api_key = \"12345abcdef\"\n-db_password = \"password123\"\n\n+api_key = os.getenv(\"API_KEY\")\n+db_password = os.getenv(\"DB_PASSWORD\")\n\n def connect_to_service():\n     '''\n-    Connects to the external service using hardcoded API key.\n+    Connects to the external service using API key from environment variables.\n     '''\n     response = requests.get(\"https://api.service.com/data\",\n-                            headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\"})\n+                            headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.getenv('API_KEY')}\"})\n     return response.json()\n\n def connect_to_database():\n```\n\nIn this diff:\n- The hardcoded `api_key` and `db_password` have been replaced with environment variables `os.getenv(\"API_KEY\")` and `os.getenv(\"DB_PASSWORD\")`.\n- Comments are updated to reflect changes in accessing API keys.\n- Ensure the necessary environment variables are set up in your development and production environments to avoid any disruptions after deploying these changes.",
